10. What is the difference between classical ABAP and ABAP on HANA?
Answer:
Classical ABAP often relies more on application-layer processing, internal tables, and traditional database access patterns. ABAP on HANA encourages pushing processing to the database using HANA-optimized SQL, CDS views, and code patterns designed for in-memory performance. The focus shifts from row-by-row processing in ABAP to set-based operations at the database layer.

